{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂enh₁-|*-lós}}
{{lbor|en|LL.|animalculum|t=lowly or small animal}} + [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|-cule|pos={{glossary|diminutive}} {{glossary|suffix}}}}. {{m|LL.||Animalculum}} is derived from {{der|en|la|animal|t=animal; living creature}} + {{m|la|-culum|pos=suffix}};<ref>{{R:OED Online|pos=n|id=7753|date=December 2022|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=n}}</ref> and {{m|la||animal}} from {{m|la|animāle}}, the {{glossary|nominative}} {{glossary|neuter}} {{glossary|singular}} of {{m|la|animālis|t=animate, living; relating to living creatures}}, from {{m|la|anima|t=breath; life; soul, spirit}} (ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*h₂enh₁-|t=to breathe}}) + {{m|la|-ālis|pos=suffix forming {{glossary|adjective}}s of relationship}}. The English word is analysable as {{suffix|en|animal|cule}}.

